course: dictionary
lesson: 4975
title: Increase: growing and adding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To increase means to become bigger in number, amount or size, or to make something bigger or more. As a noun, an increase is a rise. Look at the words around it: «increase by» tells you how much is added, and «increase to» tells you the new total.
explain: «If a predator disappears, its prey usually increases in number.» Ask yourself: do the prey animals get bigger in number? Yes, so increases means grows in number. To check, swap in grows and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths uses this word a lot. «The fare increased by 20 pence» means 20 pence is added to the old fare. «The fare increased to £2» means £2 is the new total. Look for the small word after increase: by or to.
fact: «Increase» can be a verb (to increase, it increases) or a noun (an increase).
fact: «Increase by» means add that amount; «increase to» means the new total.
fact: «On the increase» means getting bigger or more common.
fact: «A sharp increase» means a sudden, large rise.
fact: Root hairs are tiny tubes near the root tip that greatly increase the surface for taking in water.
exercise: «If a predator disappears, its prey usually increases in number.» What does increases mean here? | Stays exactly the same | *Grows in number | Gets smaller | Runs away
exercise: Maths: «The fare increased by 20 pence.» What does «increased by» tell you? | The fare is cut by 20 pence | The bus is 20 minutes late | The new fare is exactly 20 pence | *20 pence is added to the old fare
exercise: Find and copy the noun in this sentence: «There was a sharp increase in the number of stray dogs.» | *increase | number | sharp | stray
test: «Root hairs greatly increase the surface for taking in water.» Which word means nearly the same as increase here? | *Enlarge | Shrink | Waste | Freeze
test: «The number of cattle in the field increased to forty.» What does increased to forty mean? | The field is forty metres long | Forty cattle were sold | Forty cattle were added to the field | *The new total is forty
exam: «In India, stray dogs and rats increased after the vultures died.» What does increased mean? | Became fewer | *Became more in number | Stayed the same | Were banned
